\"native/jolt-file/probes/run.clj\")))}\nbb.edn:80:  probe:jolt-udp\nbb.edn:81:  {:doc \"J0b probe: raw nonblocking SOCK_DGRAM over jolt.ffi on macOS arm64 and Linux x86_64, printing the platform header first (needs bb bootstrap:jolt)\"\nbb.edn:83:           (:exit (shell {:continue true} \"sh\" \"src/dev/jolt_udp_probe.sh\")))}\nbb.edn:85:  probe:jolt-udp-failures\nbb.edn:86:  {:doc \"J7 regression probe: native UDP setup failure injection, exception/buffer cleanup, fatal error seam closure, and receive diagnostics (needs bb bootstrap:jolt)\"\nbb.edn:88:           (:exit (shell {:continue true} \"sh\" \"src/dev/jolt_udp_failures_probe.sh\")))}\nbb.edn:90:  probe:jolt-tcp\nbb.edn:91:  {:doc \"J6d: the jolt TCP substrate and owner-thread pump (dao.stream.ws.tcp, dao.stream.ws.pump, driver sleep-fds!), one child jolt process per section: closure (no jolt.socket), address (literals/localhost, resolver trap), substrate (port 0, nonblocking accept/connect, EOF vs reset, gone-peer write survives), ordered (A3 short write, drain order, failure), fairness (A1 ii/iv), stdin (A1 i, held partial line), deadline (A2 seam), control (A3 event orders, A4 pong budget, D1 close slot), close (A5, D2, D3), listener (64 cap, lower-deadlines!, drained?); native memory and registry empty after close. Arguments select sections (needs bb bootstrap:jolt)\"\nbb.edn:96:                               (println \"== probe:jolt-tcp section\" s)\nbb.edn:98:                                                \". build/tools/jolt-env.sh && exec \\\"$JOLT_HOME/bin/jolt\\\" -Srepro -M:jolt src/dev/jolt_tcp_probe.clj \\\"$1\\\"\"\nbb.edn:99:                                                \"jolt\" s))])\nbb.edn:101:           (println \"probe:jolt-tcp exits\" (pr-str results))\nbb.edn:104:  probe:jolt-ws\nbb.edn:105:  {:doc \"J6e: the jolt WebSocket host adapter (dao.stream.ws.jolt, the yin.repl.host shadow, the jolt -main wiring), one child jolt process per section: closure (C1), handshake (C2), bind (C3), address (C4), io (C5), close (C6), shutdown (C7, the real owner loop), isolation (C8), driver (C9, deadline folding, a --headless --port child), fairness (C10); native memory and registries empty after close. Arguments select sections (needs bb bootstrap:jolt and bb build:jolt-native)\"\nbb.edn:110:                               (println \"== probe:jolt-ws section\" s)\nbb.edn:112:                                                \". build/tools/jolt-env.sh && exec \\\"$JOLT_HOME/bin/jolt\\\" -Srepro -M:jolt src/dev/jolt_ws_probe.clj \\\"$1\\\"\"\nbb.edn:113:                                                \"jolt\" s))])\nbb.edn:115:           (println \"probe:jolt-ws exits\" (pr-str results))\nbb.edn:118:   workload-w:jolt\nbb.edn:119:   {:doc \"J6g: pre-registered Workload W, with an independent five-minute watchdog and ten-second sampler; one jolt worker serves two peers while stepping the REPL (needs bb bootstrap:jolt and bb build:jolt-native)\"\nbb.edn:122:                          \"exec bb src/dev/jolt_workload_w_run.clj \\\"$@\\\"\"\nbb.edn:123:                         \"jolt\" *command-line-args*)))}\nbb.edn:125:  build:jolt-native\nbb.edn:126:  {:doc \"Fetch (by pinned SHA-256, only when absent) and build the jolt-toolchain.edn :native sources with the mise-pinned CMake into build/native/<platform>/\"\nbb.edn:128:           (:exit (apply shell {:continue true} \"bb\" \"src/dev/jolt_native.clj\" *command-line-args*)))}\nbb.edn:130:  test:jolt-host\nbb.edn:131:  {:doc \"J1: the dao.host oracle (conformance, bytes, float, text tests) under jolt -Srepro -M:jolt:jolt-test through src/dev/jolt_test_runner.clj; counts per namespace, nonzero exit on any failure, error or load failure (needs bb bootstrap:jolt)\"\nbb.edn:134:                         \". build/tools/jolt-env.sh && \\\"$JOLT_HOME/bin/jolt\\\" -Srepro -M:jolt:jolt-test src/dev/jolt_test_runner.clj dao.host.conformance-test dao.host.bytes-test dao.host.float-test dao.host.text-test\")))}\nbb.edn:139:  ;; build/j2-logs/; every step is its own jolt process.\nbb.edn:140:  probe:jolt-j2\nbb.edn:141:  {:doc \"J2: staged load probe of the J2 load order under -M:jolt:jolt-test, one namespace per process (load-ok / first failing require / first unresolved symbol / first load-time error + the loaded-libs delta asserting dao.stream.transit absent); logs under build/j2-logs/probe (src/dev/jolt_j2_probe.clj; needs bb bootstrap:jolt)\"\nbb.edn:143:           (:exit (apply shell {:continue true} \"bb\" \"src/dev/jolt_j2_lane.clj\" \"probe\" *command-line-args*)))}\nbb.edn:153:  demo:jolt\nbb.edn:154:  {:doc \"J3: tracked yin.demo on JVM and jolt; require SUCCESS: sum(0..100) = 5050\"\nbb.edn:156:                                    \"bb\" \"src/dev/jolt_shell_session.clj\" \"--demo\")))}\nbb.edn:158:  test:jolt-shell\nbb.edn:159:  {:doc \"J3: one deadline-bounded transcript corpus on JVM and jolt, held stdin, exact output/exit checks and startup timings\"\nbb.edn:161:                                    \"bb\" \"src/dev/jolt_shell_session.clj\" *command-line-args*)))}\nbb.edn:163:  test:jolt-core\nbb.edn:164:  {:doc \"J2: every applicable pure suite (test/dao/host, jing, data, space, portable stream, yin/vm) under jolt, one namespace per process through src/dev/jolt_test_runner.clj, fast and ^:slow alike (Q3), nonzero exit on any failure; excluded suites are printed and recorded with reason/capability/owner\"\nbb.edn:166:           (:exit (apply shell {:continue true} \"bb\" \"src/dev/jolt_j2_lane.clj\" \"core\" *command-line-args*)))}\nbb.edn:168:  test:jolt-core:diag\nbb.edn:169:  {:doc \"J2 DIAGNOSTIC: test:jolt-core with the :jolt-diag alias added (the J1 corpus-loader stand-in for dao.jing.cbor-fixtures)\"\nbb.edn:171:           (:exit (apply shell {:continue true} \"bb\" \"src/dev/jolt_j2_lane.clj\" \"core\" \"--diag\" *command-line-args*)))}\nbb.edn:173:  test:jolt-j2-jvm\nbb.edn:174:  {:doc \"J2: the JVM counts baseline — the same included namespaces on the JVM, one process, clojure.test run-tests per namespace (src/dev/jolt_j2_jvm_runner.clj), per-namespace counts to build/j2-logs/jvm-summary.edn for the jolt-vs-JVM diff\"\nbb.edn:176:           (:exit (apply shell {:continue true} \"bb\" \"src/dev/jolt_j2_lane.clj\" \"jvm\" *command-line-args*)))}\nbb.edn:178:  test:jolt-j2-manifest\nbb.edn:179:  {:doc \"J2: self-test the applicability manifest guard with a temporary test tree; no jolt or natives needed\"\nbb.edn:181:           (:exit (shell {:continue true} \"bb\" \"src/dev/jolt_j2_manifest_check.clj\")))}\nbb.edn:183:  report:jolt-j2\nbb.edn:184:  {:doc \"J2: the jolt-vs-JVM per-namespace count table from build/j2-logs/{core,jvm}-summary.edn; runs nothing\"\nbb.edn:186:           (:exit (shell {:continue true} \"bb\" \"src/dev/jolt_j2_lane.clj\" \"report\")))}\nbb.edn:188:  test:jolt-carrier\nbb.edn:189:  {:doc \"J2: the cross-host integer-carrier test (Q1: carriers named by value). `encode` runs the JVM side (java -cp over the test:dev classpath, writes build/j2-logs/carrier-fixtures.edn); `verify` runs the jolt side (decode both rows, assert equal bytes and equal results)\"\nbb.edn:194:                                      \"mkdir -p build/j2-logs && java -cp \\\"$(clojure -Spath -A:test -A:dev)\\\" clojure.main src/dev/jolt_carrier_test.clj --encode\"))\nbb.edn:196:                                      \". build/tools/jolt-env.sh && \\\"$JOLT_HOME/bin/jolt\\\" -Srepro -M:jolt:jolt-test src/dev/jolt_carrier_test.clj --verify\"))\nbb.edn:199:  test:jolt-cbor-override\nbb.edn:202:           (:exit (apply shell {:continue true :shutdown nil} \"bb\" \"src/dev/jolt_cbor_override_check.clj\" *command-line-args*)))}\nbb.edn:204:  test:jolt-cbor-override-self-test\nbb.edn:205:  {:doc \"Self-test the CBOR override review gate in temporary worktree copies; no jolt or natives needed\"\nbb.edn:207:           (:exit (shell {:continue true :shutdown nil} \"bb\" \"src/dev/jolt_cbor_override_self_test.clj\")))}\nbb.edn:209:  test:jolt-cbor-parity\nbb.edn:210:  {:doc \"J2: differential parity of the jolt dao.stream.cbor host seam (src/jolt/dao/stream/cbor/boring.jolt) against the JVM's pinned Boring: `emit` encodes the shared corpus on the JVM (writes build/j2-logs/cbor-parity.edn), `check` re-encodes it on jolt byte-for-byte, round-trips each row and refuses a battery of non-canonical frames\"\nbb.edn:215:                                     \"mkdir -p build/j2-logs && java -cp \\\"$(clojure -Spath -A:test -A:dev)\\\" clojure.main src/dev/jolt_cbor_parity.clj --emit\"))\nbb.edn:217:                                      \". build/tools/jolt-env.sh && \\\"$JOLT_HOME/bin/jolt\\\" -Srepro -M:jolt:jolt-test src/dev/jolt_cbor_parity.clj --check\"))\nbb.edn:221:  test:jolt-text-perf\nbb.edn:222:  {:doc \"Linearity guard for the jolt dao.host.text override: code-points, unit-count, an ascending code-unit walk and utf8-encode on BMP, astral and mixed strings of 64/256/1024 Ki code points; each 4x input under 8x the time, 1024 Ki under 5 s (src/dev/jolt_text_perf.clj; needs bb bootstrap:jolt)\"\nbb.edn:225:                         \". build/tools/jolt-env.sh && \\\"$JOLT_HOME/bin/jolt\\\" -Srepro -M:jolt src/dev/jolt_text_perf.clj\")))}\nbb.edn:227:  compare:jolt-host\nbb.edn:228:  {:doc \"J1: run src/dev/jolt_profile_compare.cljc on the JVM and on jolt (public vars, arities, refusal data, a differential case battery over dao.host.*) and diff the two; writes build/j1-logs/compare-{jvm,jolt}.edn and compare.diff; exit 1 when they differ\"\nbb.edn:231:                         \"mkdir -p build/j1-logs && clojure -M src/dev/jolt_profile_compare.cljc | grep '^\\\\[' > build/j1-logs/compare-jvm.edn && . build/tools/jolt-env.sh && \\\"$JOLT_HOME/bin/jolt\\\" -Srepro -M:jolt src/dev/jolt_profile_compare.cljc | grep '^\\\\[' > build/j1-logs/compare-jolt.edn && diff build/j1-logs/compare-jvm.edn build/j1-logs/compare-jolt.edn > build/j1-logs/compare.diff; s=$?; cat build/j1-logs/compare.diff; exit $s\")))}\nbb.edn:233:  test:jolt-host-diag\nbb.edn:234:  {:doc \"J1 DIAGNOSTIC, not the oracle verdict: dao.host.float-test and dao.host.text-test, unchanged, under jolt with the :jolt-diag stand-in for the corpus loader dao.jing.cbor-fixtures (isolates these checks from the real corpus loader); see src/dev/jolt_diag/dao/jing/cbor_fixtures.cljc\"\nbb.edn:237:                         \". build/tools/jolt-env.sh && \\\"$JOLT_HOME/bin/jolt\\\" -Srepro -M:jolt:jolt-diag:jolt-test src/dev/jolt_test_runner.clj dao.host.float-test dao.host.text-test\")))}\nbb.edn:239:  test:jolt-json\nbb.edn:240:  {:doc \"J1: the jolt clojure.data.json shim (src/jolt/clojure/data/json.jolt) against src/dev/jolt_json_shim_check.cljc, under jolt; the same file passes against the real data.json on the JVM (clojure -M:dev, see its header)\"\nbb.edn:243:                         \". build/tools/jolt-env.sh && \\\"$JOLT_HOME/bin/jolt\\\" -Srepro -M:jolt:jolt-test src/dev/jolt_test_runner.clj jolt-json-shim-check\")))}\nbb.edn:245:  test:jolt-runner-self\nbb.edn:246:  {:doc \"J1: prove src/dev/jolt_test_runner.clj counts a throwing test as one error and keeps running (the jolt-runner-sentinel namespace)\"\nbb.edn:249:                         \". build/tools/jolt-env.sh && \\\"$JOLT_HOME/bin/jolt\\\" -Srepro -M:jolt:jolt-test src/dev/jolt_test_runner.clj --self-test\")))}\nbb.edn:251:  jolt:run\nbb.edn:252:  {:doc \"Run the bootstrapped jolt with build/tools/jolt-env.sh, passing every argument through (e.g. bb jolt:run -Srepro -M:jolt src/dev/jolt_j0c_workers.clj)\"\nbb.edn:255:                         \". build/tools/jolt-env.sh && exec \\\"$JOLT_HOME/bin/jolt\\\" \\\"$@\\\"\" \"jolt\"\nbb.edn:258:  build:yin-repl-node\nbb.edn:259:  {:doc \"Compile the Node yin.repl (shadow-cljs build :yin-repl) to target/yin-repl.js\"\nbb.edn:265:   :task (shell \"clj -M:cljs -m shadow.cljs.devtools.cli compile yin-repl\")}\nbb.edn:267:  build:yin-repl-peer\nbb.edn:283:             (shell \"dart compile exe lib/cljd-out/yin/repl/slice-peer.dart -o build/yin-repl-peer\"))}\nbb.edn:295:            :depends [build:yin-repl-node gen:antlr]\nbb.edn:303:             :depends [check:node-discovery build:yin-repl-node]\nbb.edn:307:             :depends [build:yin-repl-peer]\nbb.edn:312:                :depends [build:yin-repl-node gen:antlr]\nbb.edn:316:                 :depends [check:node-discovery build:yin-repl-node]\nbb.edn:321:                 :depends [build:yin-repl-peer]\nbb.edn:328:                 :depends [build:yin-repl-node gen:antlr]\nbb.edn:332:                  :depends [check:node-discovery build:yin-repl-node]\nbb.edn:343:                  :depends [build:yin-repl-peer]\nbb.edn:354:        :depends [build:yin-repl-peer build:yin-repl-node test:clj test:cljs test:cljd]}\n;; Target-aware jolt launcher seam (Lane B, astra plan C5).\n;;\n;; One place resolves HOW a jolt child process is launched, from an explicit\n;; target (default :chez, so every existing caller is unchanged):\n;;\n;;   :chez   -> \". build/tools/jolt-env.sh && exec \\\"$JOLT_HOME/bin/jolt\\\"\n;;               -Srepro -M:jolt[...] script args...\"\n;;             (the invocation every existing launcher uses today)\n;;   :gambit -> \". build/tools/jolt-env.sh && exec \\\"$JOLT_GAMBIT\\\" ...\"\n;;             (gsi resolved by bb bootstrap:jolt into JOLT_GAMBIT; the\n;;             fork's own gates invoke the same binary directly, e.g.\n;;             `sh host/gambit/ffi/watchdog.sh 120 \"$GAMBIT_GSI\"\n;;             host/gambit/gambitcheck.ss` under GAMBIT_PREFIX — see\n;;             host/gambit/ffi/README.md in the jolt checkout)\n;;\n;; Every launch exports JOLT_TARGET=<chez|gambit> into the child; the child\n;; (or the driver on its behalf) prints the identity line\n;; \"jolt-target: <target>\" and the driver ASSERTS the observed line equals the\n;; requested target before trusting any pass/fail. Absent line or mismatch is\n;; a failure (fail-closed): a Chez result can never qualify a Gambit claim.\n;;\n;; Babashka-only (bb script), like the rest of src/dev/jolt_*.\n(ns jolt-launch\n  (:require [babashka.process :as p]\n            [clojure.string :as str]))\n\n\n(def known-targets #{:chez :gambit})\n\n\n(defn resolve-target\n  \"Resolve `t` (nil, \\\"chez\\\", \\\"gambit\\\", :chez, :gambit) to a known target\n   keyword; nil answers :chez (today's default). Anything else throws.\"\n  [t]\n  (let [t (cond\n            (nil? t) :chez\n            (keyword? t) t\n            :else (keyword (str/trim (str t))))]\n    (when-not (known-targets t)\n      (throw (ex-info (str \"unknown jolt target \" (pr-str (str t))\n                           \" (known: \" (pr-str (sort (map name known-targets))) \")\")\n                      {:target t})))\n    t))\n\n\n(defn parse-target-arg\n  \"Pull [--target <t> | --target=<t>] out of `args`; answers\n   [target remaining-args]. Throws on an unknown target or a trailing bare\n   --target with no value.\"\n  [args]\n  (loop [args (vec args) target nil acc []]\n    (if (seq args)\n      (let [a (first args)]\n        (cond\n          (= \"--target\" a)\n          (do (when-not (seq (rest args))\n                (throw (ex-info \"--target needs a value (chez or gambit)\"\n                                {:arg a})))\n              (recur (subvec args 2) (resolve-target (nth args 1)) acc))\n          (str/starts-with? a \"--target=\") (recur (subvec args 1) (resolve-target (subs a 9)) acc)\n          :else (recur (subvec args 1) target (conj acc a))))\n      [(or target :chez) (vec acc)])))\n\n\n(def identity-prefix \"jolt-target: \")\n\n\n(defn identity-line\n  \"The exact identity line the CHILD prints for `target`.\"\n  [target]\n  (str identity-prefix (name (resolve-target target))))\n\n\n(defn child-target\n  \"The target a child reports for itself from its environment: JOLT_TARGET\n   when set, :chez otherwise (every existing launcher is a Chez one).\"\n  []\n  (resolve-target (System/getenv \"JOLT_TARGET\")))\n\n\n(defn launch-command\n  \"The sh -c command string that runs `script` (a path relative to the\n   repo root, or nil for stdin/-e style use) under `target`, with \\\"$@\\\"\n   carrying extra arguments. `alias` extends the -M: alias for :chez\n   (e.g. \\\"jolt-test\\\"). The child sees JOLT_TARGET so it can report its\n   own identity.\"\n  [{:keys [target script alias]}]\n  (let [target (resolve-target target)\n        alias (if (seq alias) (str \":\" alias) \"\")\n        script (if script (str \" \" script \" \"))\n        script (or script \" \")]\n    (case target\n      :chez (str \". build/tools/jolt-env.sh && export JOLT_TARGET=chez\"\n                 \" && exec \\\"$JOLT_HOME/bin/jolt\\\" -Srepro -M:jolt\" alias script \"\\\"$@\\\"\")\n      :gambit (str \". build/tools/jolt-env.sh && export JOLT_TARGET=gambit\"\n                   \" && exec \\\"$JOLT_GAMBIT\\\"\" script \"\\\"$@\\\"\"))))\n\n\n(defn run-child\n  \"Run `script` with `args` under `target` (default :chez) via\n   launch-command; answers the babashka process result map with :out/:err\n   strings. `dir` selects the working directory (default: repo root).\"\n  [{:keys [target script alias dir] :or {dir \".\"}} & args]\n  (let [cmd (launch-command {:target target :script script :alias alias})\n        r (apply p/shell {:dir dir :out :string :err :string :continue true}\n                 \"sh\" \"-c\" cmd \"jolt\" (map str args))]\n    {:exit (:exit r) :out (str (:out r)) :err (str (:err r))\n     :target (resolve-target target)}))\n\n\n(defn assert-child-target!\n  \"Fail-closed gate: `output` (the child's combined stdout+err) must contain\n   the exact identity line of `target`. Throws with a diagnosis naming the\n   observed line when the line is absent or names another host — the caller\n   must not trust any pass/fail of such a child.\"\n  [{:keys [target output context]}]\n  (let [target (resolve-target target)\n        want (identity-line target)\n        observed (some #(when (str/starts-with? % identity-prefix)\n                          (str/trim %))\n                       (str/split-lines (str output)))\n        ok? (and observed (= observed want))]\n    (when-not ok?\n      (throw (ex-info (str \"jolt child target mismatch\"\n                           (when context (str \" (\" context \")\"))\n                           \": expected \" (pr-str want)\n                           \", observed \" (pr-str observed)\n                           \" — refusing to trust this child's result\")\n                      {:wanted target :observed observed})))\n    target))\n\n\n;; The child-side identity print, for repo scripts that run UNDER jolt (where\n;; the bb seam namespace cannot load): scripts embed this one line near their\n;; entry. Silent when JOLT_TARGET is unset, so dual-host scripts (JVM leg) and\n;; legacy invocations keep their output byte-identical.\n(def child-print-snippet\n  \"(when-let [t (System/getenv \\\"JOLT_TARGET\\\")] (println (str \\\"jolt-target: \\\" t)))\")\n\n\n(def ^:private identity-probe-forms\n  {:chez \"(do (println (str \\\"jolt-target: \\\" (or (System/getenv \\\"JOLT_TARGET\\\") \\\"chez\\\"))))\"\n   :gambit \"(begin (display \\\"jolt-target: \\\")(display (or (getenv \\\"JOLT_TARGET\\\") \\\"gambit\\\"))(newline))\"})\n\n\n(defn identity-probe-form\n  \"The -e form a trivial identity child evaluates under `target` (chez:\n   bin/jolt -e evaluates Clojure; gambit: gsi -e evaluates Scheme).\"\n  [target]\n  (get identity-probe-forms (resolve-target target)))\n\n\n(defn require-chez!\n  \"Fail-closed refusal for lanes whose children are Chez-tier only (the\n   fork's Gambit FFI tier carries no native wrapper / build CLI yet —\n   host/gambit/ffi/README.md): `lane` names the refusing driver in the error.\"\n  [target lane]\n  (when (= :gambit (resolve-target target))\n    (binding [*out* *err*]\n      (println lane \"FAILED: target gambit is not qualified for this lane;\"\n               \"the Gambit FFI tier does not carry it yet\"\n               \"(jolt fork host/gambit/ffi/README.md); refusing to run\"))\n    (System/exit 1)))\n\n\n(defn preflight!\n  \"Fail-closed identity preflight for a driver: run a trivial child through\n   the same launch seam and assert it reports `target` itself, before any\n   real child's pass/fail is trusted. `context` names the driver in errors.\n   Set :identity-opt-out true for a call that runs only JVM transcript children.\"\n  ([target context] (preflight! target context {}))\n  ([target context {:keys [identity-opt-out]}]\n   (let [t (resolve-target target)]\n     (when-not (true? identity-opt-out)\n       (let [r (run-child {:target t} \"-e\" (identity-probe-form t))]\n         (assert-child-target! {:target t\n                                :output (str (:out r) (:err r))\n                                :context context})\n         (println \"PASS identity gate: child reported\" (identity-line t))))\n     t)))\n;; bb -cp src/dev src/dev/jolt_target_run.clj — the Lane B generic\n;; target-aware jolt task driver (astra plan C5). Two modes:\n;;\n;;   --script <path> [--alias <alias>] -- <child args...>\n;;       Run the repo script as a jolt child through the jolt-launch seam\n;;       (the same command string the task used before, plus the exported\n;;       JOLT_TARGET), ASSERT the child's own \"jolt-target: <target>\" line\n;;       fail-closed, and propagate its exit only after the gate passes.\n;;       The child prints the line via the seam's child-print-snippet.\n;;\n;;   (no --script) -- <args passed to the jolt binary...>\n;;       Passthrough (the old `bb jolt` behavior): an arbitrary child's\n;;       output cannot be forced to carry the identity line, so the driver\n;;       runs the fail-closed identity preflight child first and only then\n;;       passes the arguments through unchanged.\n;;\n;; --target chez (default) or --target gambit. Babashka-only.\n(ns jolt-target-run\n  (:require [jolt-launch :as jlt]))\n\n\n;; babashka does NOT flush its buffered stdout before System/exit — every\n;; relayed output must be printed AND flushed, or the child's output is lost\n;; (review round 3, P1-A).\n(defn- emit!\n  \"Print `x` to `w` (default *out*) and flush immediately.\"\n  ([x] (print x) (flush))\n  ([w x] (binding [*out* w] (print x) (flush))))\n\n\n(let [[target args] (jlt/parse-target-arg *command-line-args*)\n      [mode script alias child-args]\n      (loop [xs args script nil alias nil]\n        (cond\n          (nil? (seq xs)) [:passthrough nil nil []]\n          (= \"--script\" (first xs)) (recur (nnext xs) (second xs) alias)\n          (= \"--alias\" (first xs)) (recur (nnext xs) script (second xs))\n          (= \"--\" (first xs)) (if script\n                                [:script script alias (vec (rest xs))]\n                                [:passthrough nil nil (vec (rest xs))])\n          :else [:passthrough script alias (vec xs)]))]\n  (println \"== jolt-target-run\" (name target)\n           (when script (str \"--script \" script)))\n  (flush)\n  (if (= :script mode)\n    ;; Known repo child: assert the child's own identity line before\n    ;; trusting its exit. The child is a Clojure script, so :gambit (a bare\n    ;; gsi) cannot run it — refused fail-closed; use bb smoke:jolt-target\n    ;; for the Gambit host-scheme smoke.\n    (do (jlt/require-chez! target (str \"jolt-target-run --script \" script))\n        (let [{:keys [exit out err]} (jlt/run-child {:target target\n                                                     :script script\n                                                     :alias alias}\n                                                    child-args)\n              combined (str out err)]\n          (emit! out)\n          (emit! *err* err)\n          (flush)\n          (jlt/assert-child-target! {:target target :output combined\n                                     :context (str \"jolt-target-run --script \" script)})\n          (when-not (zero? exit)\n            (println \"jolt-target-run: child exited\" exit)\n            (flush))\n          (System/exit exit)))\n    ;; Passthrough: preflight identity gate, then hand the arguments to the\n    ;; child unchanged.\n    (let [{:keys [exit out err]} (jlt/run-child {:target target}\n                                                \"-e\" (jlt/identity-probe-form target))]\n      (jlt/assert-child-target! {:target target\n                                 :output (str out err)\n                                 :context \"jolt-target-run passthrough preflight\"})\n      (emit! (str out \"\\n\"))\n      (when-not (zero? exit)\n        (println \"jolt-target-run: preflight child exited\" exit)\n        (flush)\n        (System/exit exit))\n      (println \"PASS identity gate: child reported\" (jlt/identity-line target))\n      (flush)\n      ;; The real child, byte-identical command shape, exit propagated.\n      (let [{:keys [exit out err]} (apply jlt/run-child\n                                          {:target target}\n                                          child-args)]\n        (emit! out)\n        (emit! *err* err)\n        (flush)\n        (System/exit exit)))))\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
