{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_10","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"cat jolt-toolchain.edn && sed -n '40,150p;355,376p' src/dev/jolt_bootstrap.clj && cat .mise.local.toml 2>/dev/null\"","aggregated_output":";; The jolt host lane's toolchain declaration (owner fork pin, 2026-10-22)\n;; (docs/design/yin.repl-jolt-implementation.md §6.1, §6.4).\n;;\n;; `bb bootstrap:jolt` materializes exactly this into build/tools/jolt and\n;; verifies it; ordinary runs never pull. Pin changes use the upgrade gate\n;; (`qualify:jolt-upgrade`, §6.4), with the explicit exception recorded below.\n{:jolt\n {:origin \"https://github.com/sonwh98/jolt\"\n  :sha \"f22df3c70dce4e7f725df580daa8991a41420660\"\n  :committed \"2026-11-20T05:00:00+07:00\"\n  ;; owner decision 2026-10-22, pinned ahead of the first qualify:jolt-upgrade\n  ;; run (section 6.4 ruling 4 exception); requalified by the manual section 6\n  ;; checklist (collab review 1792692000000)\n  :tag :none\n  :nearest-release-tag {:tag \"v0.8.23\"\n                        :sha \"a0ac71c3f638fe55158bd01b4ecbb0dd3d7545e5\"}\n  :describe \"gambit-ffi-p1c-f22df3c7\"\n  :dir \"build/tools/jolt\"\n  ;; recursive submodule SHAs at :sha (git submodule status --recursive);\n  ;; bootstrap refuses a checkout whose submodules differ\n  :submodules {\"vendor/cli\" \"14f07644080070246974942415a104228d9a6b04\"\n               \"vendor/clojure-test-suite\" \"489b6743e8421687ef96cec557830acf258d1886\"\n               \"vendor/fs\" \"5b273b8a943a622593fbc85fca6761c5a39d6d66\"\n               \"vendor/grenadine\" \"688e0ed6618582eccc8c8b745243ceac92835e03\"\n               \"vendor/irregex\" \"c948a704fc732914a243c1643bfe359913d11c7b\"\n               \"vendor/process\" \"43bdd65e189f2ccacc56662c53a21f5470ff1500\"\n               \"vendor/sci\" \"32d62a5136ad3dc148588752f5bcc4cc30b14752\"}\n  ;; The fork pin carries the Sorted fix: sonwh98/jolt#2, source 7b7100c1\n  ;; and regenerated seeds 697b91ee. No bootstrap patch or re-mint is needed.\n  ;; Re-pinned 2026-10-24 (owner ruling: the JVM is canonical, jolt-lang is\n  ;; patched via the fork, same exception as 2026-10-22) to b389f1a7 on fork\n  ;; branch assoc-deftype-refusal, one commit on 697b91ee: assoc on a deftype\n  ;; that is not Associative throws ClassCastException, as on the JVM\n  ;; (host/chez/records-coll.ss; seeds unchanged at the remint byte-fixpoint;\n  ;; format-patch SHA-256 776019b9954113c13a74c7e8fce309040e33a99da859a9620701a9f094513c9f;\n  ;; upstream report text in collab/1792824446211-engineer-canonical-adjudication-fixes...).\n  ;; Former patch 0001-sorted-user-types (base 96d7b866) is retired;\n  ;; the patch mechanism stays available for future patches.\n  ;; Re-pinned 2026-11-20 (owner-directed) to dd605630 on fork branch\n  ;; gambit-ffi-p1b: the Gambit FFI stage-1 tier (loader/memory/ordinary\n  ;; calls/errno qualified on macOS arm64 + Linux x86_64; blocking,\n  ;; foreign-thread callbacks and dynamic callables keep honest refusals;\n  ;; jolt CI code-green on Linux + Android shards) PLUS the pinned\n  ;; assoc-deftype refusal fix carried as commit dd605630 (cherry-picked from\n  ;; b389f1a7; unit row records-assoc-refusal at test/chez/unit.edn:2596\n  ;; gate-holds the parity: [false \"class user.AssocRefusal cannot be cast to\n  ;; class clojure.lang.Associative\"]; seeds byte-identical). Submodule pins\n  ;; unchanged from b389f1a7. Evidence: collab/jolt/1795108300000-*\n  ;; (p1b-stage1/P1b-assoc-parity.findings.md in the clone); gate matrix in\n  ;; collab/jolt/1795042000000-* findings. Advanced 2026-11-20 (same owner direction) to f22df3c7 on fork branch\n  ;; gambit-ffi-p1c: yin.repl RUNNING under the Gambit backend — real yin>\n  ;; session (12 replies: evaluation, error handling, frontend refusal,\n  ;; qualified FFI call, blocking-ffi C4 refusal inline, clean quit) via the\n  ;; gambityinrepl gate on BOTH platforms (macOS arm64 + Linux x86_64; the\n  ;; Linux compiled-boot heap issue resolved as a missing DATOMWORLD_ROOT\n  ;; default, now fail-closed preflight). Cross-family review: glm-5.3-flash\n  ;; ACCEPT (gate honesty verified by re-run; collab/jolt/1795135000000-*).\n  :patches []}\n\n ;; Host OS packages (owner 2026-10-20: Linux = the Debian family with apt).\n ;; `bb bootstrap:jolt` checks :required with dpkg-query on hosts whose\n ;; /etc/os-release ID or ID_LIKE names debian, BEFORE anything mise builds,\n ;; and fails naming the missing packages and the exact\n ;; `sudo apt-get install -y ...` command. It never runs sudo or apt.\n ;; :unverified entries are candidates with no step shown to need them yet;\n ;; they are listed, not checked. Chez and CMake stay mise-provided.\n :os-packages\n {:debian\n  {:required\n   {;; mise builds Chez 10.4.1 from source and links it against ncurses;\n    ;; verified on shiva (Ubuntu 24.04.5): \"cannot find -lncurses\" until\n    ;; this was installed (docs/orchestrator-log.md, J0b-on-shiva entry)\n    \"libncurses-dev\" \"mise Chez source build (link)\"\n    ;; Chez's expression editor (c/expeditor.c:1189-1212) reads the X11\n    ;; clipboard; verified on jupiter (Ubuntu 24.04.5): the build failed with\n    ;; \"c/expeditor.c:1191: fatal error: X11/Xlib.h: No such file or\n    ;; directory\" until this was installed (shiva had the headers already,\n    ;; so it never failed there). Chez's configure also offers --disable-x11\n    ;; and --disable-curses, which the mise plugin does not pass.\n    \"libx11-dev\" \"mise Chez source build (compile, X11 clipboard in the editor)\"\n    ;; the same Chez source build compiles and links C (the failing step\n    ;; above was its link); present on shiva, so not independently shown\n    \"gcc\" \"mise Chez source build (C compiler)\"\n    \"make\" \"mise Chez source build (make)\"\n    ;; bootstrap:jolt clones jolt and its submodules (src/dev/jolt_bootstrap.clj)\n    \"git\" \"bootstrap:jolt clone and verification\"\n    ;; J1b: native/jolt-crypto compiles against the libcrypto headers\n    ;; (openssl/evp.h) and links the declared :native :libcrypto path\n    \"libssl-dev\" \"J1b native build (libcrypto headers and link, native/jolt-crypto)\"}\n   ;; J1b runtime: the package owning the declared libcrypto.so.3 differs per\n   ;; release, so any ONE of these satisfies it (dpkg -S on shiva, Ubuntu\n   ;; 24.04: libssl3t64; Debian bookworm and Ubuntu 22.04: libssl3). Checked\n   ;; by `bb build:jolt-native`, not by `bb bootstrap:jolt` (which checks\n   ;; :required only). The library itself is checked against :native\n   ;; :libcrypto :qualified.\n   :runtime-any-of\n   {\"libcrypto.so.3 (J1b dao.host.hash/sign)\" [\"libssl3t64\" \"libssl3\"]}\n   :unverified\n   {;; J0c native build (jolt-j0c branch, bb build:jolt-native) compiles the\n    ;; ANTLR4 C++ runtime and wrapper and unzips the runtime source; shown on\n    ;; macOS only, not yet on a Debian host\n    \"g++\" \"J0c native build (C++ compiler)\"\n    \"unzip\" \"J0c native build (runtime source archive)\"}}\n  ;; Homebrew is assumed on macOS and not enforced; the libcrypto it provides\n  ;; is checked by path and version instead (:native :libcrypto, J1b).\n  :macos {:manager :homebrew :enforced false\n          :packages {\"openssl@3\" \"libcrypto for dao.host.hash/sign (J1b)\"}}}\n\n ;; Provisioned by mise from the exact pins in mise.toml. JOLT_CHEZ is always\n ;; set explicitly (build/tools/jolt-env.sh), never left to jolt's PATH search.\n :chez {:version \"10.4.1\"\n        :provider :mise\n        :mise-tool \"chezscheme\"\n        :threaded true\n        :binary \"bin/scheme\"}\n ;; Gambit host (jolt host/gambit gates, G1): built from source by mise via the\n ;; asdf plugin joeljuca/asdf-gambit (mise.toml) at the exact pin — the same\n ;; from-source 4.9.8 jolt's CI gates target. Only gsi is needed by the gates\n ;; (the Makefile passes GAMBIT_PREFIX/bin/gsi); JOLT_GAMBIT is set explicitly\n ;; in build/tools/jolt-env.sh, never left to a PATH search (gsc on PATH is\n ;; Ghostscript).\n :gambit {:version \"4.9.8\"\n          :provider :mise\n          :mise-tool \"gambit\"\n          :binary \"bin/gsi\"}\n :cmake {:version \"4.4.4\"\n         :provider :mise\n         :mise-tool \"cmake\"}\n\n ;; Recorded at J0a round 1 on the platforms actually run.\n :observed\n {:macos-arm64 {:os \"macOS 26.6.2 (25G83)\"\n                :chez-path \"~/.local/share/mise/installs/chezscheme/10.4.1/bin/scheme\"\n                :cmake-path \"~/.local/share/mise/installs/cmake/4.4.4/cmake-4.4.4-macos-universal/CMake.app/Contents/bin/cmake\"\n                :cc \"Apple clang version 21.0.0 (clang-2100.1.1.101)\"\n                ;; J1b, 2026-10-21 (Homebrew openssl@3)\n                :libcrypto {:path \"/opt/homebrew/opt/openssl@3/lib/libcrypto.3.dylib\"\n                            :resolved \"/opt/homebrew/Cellar/openssl@3/3.6.3/lib/libcrypto.3.dylib\"\n                            :version \"OpenSSL 3.6.3 9 Jun 2026\"}}\n  ;; shiva.stigmergy.systems, J1b 2026-10-21 (scratch clone ~/ci/datomworld-jolt-j1b)\n  :linux-x86_64 {:os \"Ubuntu 24.04.5 LTS (kernel 6.8.0-147-generic)\"\n                 :chez-path \"~/.local/share/mise/installs/chezscheme/10.4.1/bin/scheme\"\n                 :cmake-path \"~/.local/share/mise/installs/cmake/4.4.4/cmake-4.4.4-linux-x86_64/bin/cmake\"\n                 :cc \"cc (Ubuntu 13.3.0-6ubuntu2~24.04.1) 13.3.0\"\n                 :libcrypto {:path \"/usr/lib/x86_64-linux-gnu/libcrypto.so.3\"\n                             :resolved \"/usr/lib/x86_64-linux-gnu/libcrypto.so.3\"\n                             :version \"OpenSSL 3.0.13 30 Jan 2024\"\n                             :package \"libssl3t64 3.0.13-0ubuntu3.16\"}}}\n\n ;; Vendored native sources (§6.1, Q4): fetched by `bb build:jolt-native`\n ;; only when absent from build/native/src, accepted only at the pinned\n ;; SHA-256, built with the mise-pinned CMake into build/native/<platform>/.\n ;; Nothing downloads during namespace loading. :libcrypto is the one system\n ;; (not vendored) entry: declared by path and minimum version, never fetched.\n :native\n {:antlr4-cpp-runtime\n  {:version \"4.13.2\"\n   :license \"BSD-3-Clause\"\n   ;; the official C++ runtime source distribution (antlr4 doc/cpp-target.md);\n   ;; the GitHub release carries no C++ asset\n   :url \"https://www.antlr.org/download/antlr4-cpp-runtime-4.13.2-source.zip\"\n   :sha256 \"0ed13668906e86dbc0dcddf30fdee68c10203dea4e83852b4edb810821bee3c4\"\n   :upstream {:repo \"https://github.com/antlr/antlr4\"\n              :tag \"4.13.2\"\n              :tag-object \"2ac185af855ff39b4b8c41854b756767099c356f\"\n              :commit \"cc82115a4e7f53d71d9d905caa2c2dfa4da58899\"\n              :path \"runtime/Cpp\"}\n   ;; static, position-independent: linked into the one wrapper dylib that\n   ;; jolt loads, so no second library or rpath is resolved at load time.\n   ;; Tests off: ANTLR_BUILD_CPP_TESTS=ON downloads googletest at configure\n   ;; time.\n   :cmake-flags [\"-DCMAKE_BUILD_TYPE=Release\"\n                 \"-DANTLR_BUILD_CPP_TESTS=OFF\"\n                 \"-DANTLR_BUILD_SHARED=OFF\"\n                 \"-DANTLR_BUILD_STATIC=ON\"\n                 \"-DCMAKE_POSITION_INDEPENDENT_CODE=ON\"\n                 \"-DCMAKE_CXX_STANDARD=17\"]}\n\n  ;; §6.2: the upstream BLAKE3 C reference (c/ of the release), built static\n  ;; and position-independent and linked into native/jolt-crypto. Portable C\n  ;; only (BLAKE3_SIMD_TYPE=none, the option name verified in c/CMakeLists.txt\n  ;; at this tag); SIMD is a later, separately measured change.\n  :blake3\n  {:version \"1.8.7\"\n   :license \"CC0-1.0 OR Apache-2.0 OR Apache-2.0 WITH LLVM-exception\"\n   ;; GitHub's tag archive; downloaded twice 2026-10-21, both SHA-256 equal\n   :url \"https://github.com/BLAKE3-team/BLAKE3/archive/refs/tags/1.8.7.tar.gz\"\n   :sha256 \"c6782a28842b1c0478524ac06a4f2ede784038ee298d6e2162c0b089c4306a3c\"\n   ;; saved under build/native/src by this name (the URL ends in 1.8.7.tar.gz)\n   :archive-name \"BLAKE3-1.8.7.tar.gz\"\n   :upstream {:repo \"https://github.com/BLAKE3-team/BLAKE3\"\n              :tag \"1.8.7\"\n              ;; a lightweight tag: refs/tags/1.8.7 names the commit directly\n              :commit \"f3149ec5bb5449af877ba20377a11008ff499fa2\"\n              :released \"2026-08-20T09:06:20Z\"\n              :path \"c\"}\n   :cmake-flags [\"-DCMAKE_BUILD_TYPE=Release\"\n                 \"-DBUILD_SHARED_LIBS=OFF\"\n                 \"-DCMAKE_POSITION_INDEPENDENT_CODE=ON\"\n                 \"-DCMAKE_INSTALL_LIBDIR=lib\"\n                 \"-DBLAKE3_SIMD_TYPE=none\"\n                 \"-DBLAKE3_USE_TBB=OFF\"\n                 \"-DBLAKE3_FETCH_TBB=OFF\"\n                 \"-DBUILD_TESTING=OFF\"]}\n\n  ;; §6.3 / Q4: the SYSTEM libcrypto, never vendored. native/jolt-crypto links\n  ;; it by :path (install name on macOS, -rpath on Linux). Never Apple's\n  ;; libcrypto (it aborts inside EVP_Digest).\n  ;;\n  ;; :qualified is the one library per platform that passed the J1b gates:\n  ;; its canonical real path, exact OpenSSL_version_num and the SHA-256 of\n  ;; the file. Any difference fails closed until requalified, so a Homebrew\n  ;; or apt upgrade (new version, and on Homebrew a repointed opt/ link), and\n  ;; a same-path, same-version package replacement (new digest) all refuse:\n  ;;   * `bb build:jolt-native` (check-libcrypto!) fails on a canonical path\n  ;;     or digest that differs (it cannot read the version without loading\n  ;;     the library);\n  ;;   * loading dao.host.hash fails on canonical path, version or digest, as\n  ;;     the wrapper reports them for the library the EVP entries resolved to.\n  ;; :min-version is separate: the lowest version a requalification may\n  ;; accept.\n  ;;\n  ;; Requalification (the upgrade gate, §6.4), on the platform that changed:\n  ;;   1. `bb build:jolt-native --requalify` (builds against the changed\n  ;;      library; skips only the :qualified comparison, and says so in the\n  ;;      build record);\n  ;;   2. `bb qualify:jolt-libcrypto` prints the observed {:canonical-path\n  ;;      :version-num :version :sha256} (the digest computed by bb and by\n  ;;      the library, required equal; the version at least :min-version)\n  ;;      and changes nothing;\n  ;;   3. replace this platform's :qualified entry with it, review the diff;\n  ;;   4. `bb build:jolt-native`, `bb compare:jolt-host`, `bb\n  ;;      probe:jolt-crypto`, all of which must pass.\n  :libcrypto\n  {:provider :system\n   :soname {:darwin-arm64 \"libcrypto.3.dylib\" :linux-x86_64 \"libcrypto.so.3\"}\n   :path {:darwin-arm64 \"/opt/homebrew/opt/openssl@3/lib/libcrypto.3.dylib\"\n          :linux-x86_64 \"/usr/lib/x86_64-linux-gnu/libcrypto.so.3\"}\n   :include {:darwin-arm64 \"/opt/homebrew/opt/openssl@3/include\"\n             :linux-x86_64 \"/usr/include\"}\n   :min-version \"3.0.0\"\n   ;; qualified 2026-10-21 (J1b): macOS from this checkout, Linux on shiva\n   :qualified\n   {:darwin-arm64 {:canonical-path \"/opt/homebrew/Cellar/openssl@3/3.6.3/lib/libcrypto.3.dylib\"\n                   :version-num 811597872\n                   :version \"OpenSSL 3.6.3 9 Jun 2026\"\n                   :sha256 \"a12805a18cd5e4f733fa8727b91afa08b587f9da5a760517cd79cb508a3a3f71\"}\n    :linux-x86_64 {:canonical-path \"/usr/lib/x86_64-linux-gnu/libcrypto.so.3\"\n                   :version-num 805306576\n                   :version \"OpenSSL 3.0.13 30 Jan 2024\"\n                   :sha256 \"6866ed711dab8927e1bf82bf1cd30e828bdfc34f3cc1e83b1c9eb01ce6c37d9a\"}}\n   ;; Debian runtime packages: checked by `bb build:jolt-native`, NOT by\n   ;; `bb bootstrap:jolt` (which checks only :os-packages :debian :required,\n   ;; libssl-dev among them); macOS: Homebrew openssl@3, unenforced\n   :debian-runtime-any-of [\"libssl3t64\" \"libssl3\"]}}}\n\n(defn- sh\n  \"Run a command, answer trimmed stdout; fail the task on a nonzero exit.\"\n  [& args]\n  (let [opts (if (map? (first args)) (first args) {})\n        cmd (if (map? (first args)) (rest args) args)\n        r (apply p/shell (merge {:out :string :err :string :continue true} opts) cmd)]\n    (when-not (zero? (:exit r))\n      (fail! (str/join \" \" cmd) \" exited \" (:exit r) \"\\n\" (:err r)\n             \"\\nRemedy: git -C build/tools/jolt checkout -- . && bb bootstrap:jolt\"))\n    (str/trim (:out r))))\n\n\n(defn- mise-bin\n  \"The path of executable `exe` from mise tool `tool` at exactly `version`\n   (mise's own resolution: the layout differs per platform).\"\n  [tool version exe]\n  (let [r (p/shell {:out :string :err :string :continue true}\n                   \"mise\" \"exec\" (str tool \"@\" version) \"--\" \"which\" exe)]\n    (when-not (zero? (:exit r))\n      (fail! \"mise has no \" tool \"@\" version \" installed; run `mise install \" tool \"`\"))\n    (str/trim (:out r))))\n\n\n(defn- check-chez\n  [{:keys [version binary threaded]}]\n  (let [scheme (mise-bin \"chezscheme\" version (str (fs/file-name binary)))\n        v (sh scheme \"--version\")\n        t (sh {:in \"(display (threaded?))\"} scheme \"-q\")]\n    (when-not (= version v) (fail! \"Chez at \" scheme \" reports \" v \", pinned \" version))\n    (when (and threaded (not= \"#t\" t)) (fail! \"Chez at \" scheme \" is not threaded\"))\n    (println \"chez\" v \"threaded\" t scheme)\n    scheme))\n\n\n(defn- check-gambit\n  \"Analogous to check-chez: resolve gsi through mise at the exact pin, require\n   the reported version (system-version-string, e.g. \\\"v4.9.8\\\") to equal the\n   pin, and smoke the interpreter. Required, not warned: mise.toml pins gambit\n   for every host, so `mise install` provisions it before this runs, and the\n   jolt Gambit gates (Makefile GAMBIT_PREFIX targets) are part of the lane —\n   bootstrapping without it would silently leave JOLT_GAMBIT unset.\"\n  [{:keys [version binary]}]\n  (let [gsi (mise-bin \"gambit\" version (str (fs/file-name binary)))\n        v (sh gsi \"-e\" \"(display (system-version-string))\")\n        t (sh gsi \"-e\" \"(display (+ 1 2))\")]\n    (when-not (= (str \"v\" version) v)\n      (fail! \"Gambit at \" gsi \" reports \" v \", pinned \" version))\n    (when-not (= \"3\" t) (fail! \"Gambit at \" gsi \" failed the interpreter smoke\"))\n    (println \"gambit\" v gsi)\n    gsi))\n\n\n(defn- check-cmake\n  [{:keys [version]}]\n  (let [cmake (mise-bin \"cmake\" version \"cmake\")\n        v (first (str/split-lines (sh cmake \"--version\")))]\n    (when-not (= (str \"cmake version \" version) v)\n      (fail! \"CMake at \" cmake \" reports \" v \", pinned \" version))\n    (println v cmake)\n    cmake))\n\n\n(defn- submodule-shas\n  [dir]\n  ;; Not through `sh`: its trim would eat the status column of the first line\n  ;; (\" \" checked out at the recorded commit, \"-\" uninitialized, \"+\" differs).\n  (let [r (p/shell {:out :string :err :string :continue true}\n                   \"git\" \"-C\" dir \"submodule\" \"status\" \"--recursive\")]\n    (when-not (zero? (:exit r)) (fail! \"git submodule status: \" (:err r)))\n    (into {}\n          (map (fn [line]\n                 (let [[sha path] (str/split (str/trim (subs line 1)) #\"\\s+\")]\n                   (when (not= \\space (first line))\n                     (fail! \"submodule \" path \" is not checked out at its recorded commit: \" line))\n                   [path sha])))\n          (remove str/blank? (str/split-lines (:out r))))))\n\n\n(defn- materialize!\n  [{:keys [origin sha dir]}]\n  (when-not (fs/exists? dir)\n    (fs/create-dirs (fs/parent dir))\n    (println \"cloning\" origin \"into\" dir)\n    (sh \"git\" \"clone\" \"--no-checkout\" origin dir)\n    (sh \"git\" \"-C\" dir \"checkout\" \"--detach\" sha)\n    (sh \"git\" \"-C\" dir \"submodule\" \"update\" \"--init\" \"--recursive\")))\n\n\n(defn- verify!\n  [{:keys [origin sha dir submodules]}]\n  (let [head (sh \"git\" \"-C\" dir \"rev-parse\" \"HEAD\")\n        remote (sh \"git\" \"-C\" dir \"remote\" \"get-url\" \"origin\")\n        remedy (str \"\\nRemedy: git -C build/tools/jolt checkout -- .\"\n                    \" && git -C build/tools/jolt remote set-url origin \" origin\n                    \" && git -C build/tools/jolt fetch origin \" sha\n                    \" && git -C build/tools/jolt checkout --detach \" sha\n                    \" && git -C build/tools/jolt submodule update --init --recursive\"\n                    \" && bb bootstrap:jolt\"\n                    \"\\nAlternatively: rm -rf build/tools/jolt && bb bootstrap:jolt\"\n                    \"\\nPin changes go through qualify:jolt-upgrade.\")]\n    (when-not (= origin remote)\n      (fail! dir \" has origin \" remote \", declared \" origin remedy))\n    (when-not (= sha head)\n      (fail! dir \" is at \" head \", declared \" sha remedy))\n    (let [actual (submodule-shas dir)]\n      (when-not (= submodules actual)\n        (fail! \"submodule SHAs differ from jolt-toolchain.edn: \" (pr-str actual))))\n    (println \"jolt\" head \"with\" (count submodules) \"submodules verified\")))\n\n\n(defn -main\n  [& _]\n  (let [{:keys [jolt chez gambit cmake os-packages]} (edn/read-string (slurp \"jolt-toolchain.edn\"))\n        _ (check-os-packages os-packages)\n        scheme (check-chez chez)\n        gsi (check-gambit gambit)\n        _ (check-cmake cmake)\n        dir (str (fs/absolutize (or (System/getenv \"JOLT_BOOTSTRAP_TEST_DIR\") (:dir jolt))))\n        jolt (assoc jolt :dir dir)\n        env-file (str (fs/path (fs/parent dir) \"jolt-env.sh\"))]\n    (materialize! jolt)\n    (verify! jolt)\n    (let [record (apply-patches! jolt scheme)]\n      (spit env-file\n            (str \"# written by bb bootstrap:jolt from jolt-toolchain.edn; do not edit\\n\"\n                 \"export JOLT_CHEZ='\" scheme \"'\\n\"\n                 \"export JOLT_GAMBIT='\" gsi \"'\\n\"\n                 \"export JOLT_HOME='\" dir \"'\\n\"\n                 \"export JOLT_PATCHES='\" record \"'\\n\"))\n      (println \"wrote\" env-file))))\n\n\n","exit_code":1,"status":"failed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_11","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"rg --files src | rg 'yin/(shell/main|repl/(main|slice_peer|frontends)).*\\\\.(clj|cljc|jolt)\"'$'\"' && sed -n '1,115p' src/cljc/yin/shell/main.cljc && sed -n '1,68p' src/cljc/yin/vm/docs/yin.repl.md && rg -n 'defn -main|command-line-args|read-line|exit' src/cljc/yin/repl/slice_peer.cljc\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_11","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"rg --files src | rg 'yin/(shell/main|repl/(main|slice_peer|frontends)).*\\\\.(clj|cljc|jolt)\"'$'\"' && sed -n '1,115p' src/cljc/yin/shell/main.cljc && sed -n '1,68p' src/cljc/yin/vm/docs/yin.repl.md && rg -n 'defn -main|command-line-args|read-line|exit' src/cljc/yin/repl/slice_peer.cljc\"","aggregated_output":"src/cljc/yin/repl/frontends.cljc\nsrc/cljc/yin/repl/main.cljc\nsrc/cljc/yin/shell/main.cljc\n(ns yin.shell.main\n  \"The outer host entry point: the engine's driver plus this project's\n   storage composition.\n\n   `yin.repl.main` is the engine's host driver — cadence, one step owner,\n   the line producers and the bounded shutdown drain — and it names no\n   transport, no peer, no key file and no store past `mem` and `file:<dir>`.\n   Everything past that reaches it as one plain-data value, `composition`,\n   assembled here out of the composition's own namespaces: the command line\n   (`yin.shell.cli`), the store factory (`yin.shell.store`), the session\n   where the section 7 adapters meet the engine (`yin.shell.session`), and\n   the DHT composition's transport lifecycle (`yin.shell.dht`).\n\n   This is the namespace the shipped binaries run — `deps.edn`'s\n   `:clj-yin-repl` and `:jolt-yin-repl`, shadow-cljs's `:yin-repl` build and\n   the ClojureDart `:main` — and it is why the engine's own dependency\n   closure can stay free of a storage implementation\n   (docs/design/yin.repl.dht-composition.md sections 2, 6 and 10, Gate A):\n   the require runs this way, and never the other way round.  `yin.shell.cli`\n   consumes the engine driver's primitives (`parse-int`, `plain-args`); the\n   engine driver consumes nothing of a composition's except the value handed\n   to it, so there is no cycle to break and nothing to resolve at runtime.\n\n   This namespace owns no socket, atom, promise, callback, clock or namespace\n   global of its own: `composition` is one constant map of function values,\n   and each host's `-main` is a single call into the engine driver's `main!`.\"\n  (:require [yin.repl.main :as repl.main]\n            [yin.shell.cli :as cli]\n            [yin.shell.dht :as shell.dht]\n            [yin.shell.session :as shell.session]\n            [yin.shell.store :as shell.store]))\n\n\n(def composition\n  \"The plain-data bundle this project's hosts hand `yin.repl.main` as its\n   `:composition`: every key that driver documents, and nothing that reaches\n   past it.\n\n   The command-line half is `yin.shell.cli/hooks` — the flags, the\n   subcommands, the key file, the help and the banner text.  The rest is the\n   store and its transport lifecycle, each entry one function value taken\n   statically from the namespace that owns it, so the wiring is identical on\n   the JVM, on Node and on Dart and no host resolves a symbol at runtime\n   (docs/design/yin.repl.dht-composition.md sections 6 and 7).\n\n   The lifecycle functions all take the one composition session\n   `{:engine … :node … :key …}` and are driven by the engine driver's single\n   tick: `:step` advances the transport and answers its lines and its own\n   events, `:recheck-on-tick` serves the link and call media the engine\n   parks on and translates those events before they cross inward, and\n   `:stop!`/`:stopped?`/`:close!` are the one resource owner's exit — asked\n   once, completed by `:step`, and forced only by the drain's last resort.\"\n  (merge (cli/hooks)\n         {:composition-spec? shell.store/composition-spec?\n          :open shell.store/open\n          :close-store! shell.store/close!\n          :step shell.dht/step\n          :recheck-on-tick shell.session/recheck-on-tick\n          :recheck-after-input shell.session/recheck-after-input\n          :stop! shell.dht/stop!\n          :stopped? shell.dht/stopped?\n          :close! shell.dht/close!\n          :busy? shell.dht/busy?\n          :refusal shell.dht/refusal\n          :admitting? shell.dht/admitting?\n          :startup-lines shell.dht/follow-lines}))\n\n\n#?(:cljd nil\n   :jolt nil\n   :clj\n   (defn -main\n     \"The shipped JVM entry point: the engine's driver over `composition`.\"\n     [& args]\n     (repl.main/main! args composition)))\n\n\n#?(:jolt\n   (defn -main\n     \"The shipped jolt entry point: the engine's driver over `composition`.\"\n     [& args]\n     (repl.main/main! args composition)))\n\n\n#?(:cljs\n   (defn -main\n     \"The shipped Node entry point: the engine's driver over `composition`.\"\n     [& args]\n     (repl.main/main! args composition)))\n\n\n#?(:cljd\n   (do\n     (defn -main\n       \"The shipped Dart entry point: the engine's driver over `composition`.\"\n       [& args]\n       (repl.main/main! args composition))\n\n     (defn ^{:dart/name main} run-main\n       [args]\n       (apply -main args))))\n\n\n(defn startup\n  \"Parse the arguments and compose the shell with this project's\n   shipped storage composition.\"\n  ([args] (repl.main/startup args {:composition composition}))\n  ([args opts] (repl.main/startup args (assoc opts :composition composition))))\n\n\n(defn parse-args\n  \"Parse the arguments using this project's shipped storage composition.\"\n  [args]\n  (repl.main/parse-args args composition))\n\n# yin.repl: Quick Start & User Guide\n\n`yin.repl` is the primary user interface into datom.world. It is a cross-host\nshell (JVM, Node, Dart, and Jolt) that evaluates code on `yin.vm`, serves and\nconnects to remote shells over WebSockets, and composes with `dao.jing.dht` to\npublish and load modules by signed name over a distributed hash table (DHT).\nThe same CLI, flags and index-store schemes work on every host; only the\nlaunch command differs (section 1.1).\n\n---\n\n## 1. Quick Start: Launching the REPL\n\n### Launch on each host\n\nThe engine, flags and `--index-store` schemes are identical on all four hosts;\neach host differs only in how the shell starts.\n\n**JVM** (the reference host; every flag is exercised here first):\n\n```bash\nclj -M:clj-yin-repl\n```\n\n**Node** (a self-contained `node-script` build; the first build needs the\ngenerated JS parser, which `bb build:yin-repl-node` produces):\n\n```bash\nbb build:yin-repl-node     # compiles the shadow-cljs :yin-repl build\nnode target/yin-repl.js --index-store mem\n```\n\n**Dart** (ClojureDart compiles the shell to a Dart script):\n\n```bash\nclj -M:clojuredart:cljd-yin-repl-build    # emits build/yin-repl/yin_repl.dart\ndart run build/yin-repl/yin_repl.dart --index-store mem\n```\n\n**Jolt** (the native Chez host; the bootstrap materializes the pinned jolt and\nits stdlib — run it once per checkout, then always launch through\n`build/tools/jolt-env.sh` so `$JOLT_HOME/bin` leads PATH; a system/Homebrew\njolt lacks the J6-era stdlib modules):\n\n```bash\nbb bootstrap:jolt\n. build/tools/jolt-env.sh\nexport PATH=\"$JOLT_HOME/bin:$PATH\"\njolt -Srepro -M:jolt:jolt-yin-repl --index-store mem\n```\n\nPer-host store status for `--index-store`: `mem` everywhere; `file:<dir>` on\nJVM, Node, Dart and Jolt (J4+); `dht:<dir>` on JVM, Node, Dart, and on Jolt\nsince the J7 slices 1-2 (2026-11-15; the sections 6-7 process/interop gate of\nyin.repl-jolt-implementation.md §10.1 remains open). `--help` works on every\nhost.\n\n### Local In-Memory REPL\nStart an interactive prompt on the JVM with an in-memory index store:\n\n```bash\nclj -M:clj-yin-repl\n```\n\n> **Note for fresh clones:** `yin.repl` loads the generated ANTLR Python3 parser on startup. Run `bb gen:antlr` (or `clj -M:antlr-gen` for JVM) once before starting the REPL or running tests.\n\n### Durable Local Store\nTo persist definitions and evaluated code across restarts, pass a `file:` directory store:\nrg: src/cljc/yin/repl/slice_peer.cljc: IO error for operation on src/cljc/yin/repl/slice_peer.cljc: No such file or directory (os error 2)\n","exit_code":2,"status":"failed"}}
