{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_105","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"git -C build/p1d-tools/jolt show HEAD:p1c/P1c.findings.md | sed -n '175,215p'; sed -n '1,75p' collab/jolt/1795135000000-reviewer-p1c-glm.glm-5.3-flash.findings.md; tail -3 /tmp/p1d-gambit.log\"","aggregated_output":"trace reached 138 namespace-ready markers, then all 12 expected replies in\norder including `yin> Bye`. `/usr/bin/time` measured 722,836 KiB peak RSS\nand 299.46s elapsed, with launcher status 0. The gate's own AWK assertions\npassed on that transcript. The shorter diagnostic deadlines expired during\nordinary namespace loading. The successful run establishes bounded resource\nuse for this acceptance corpus with Gambit's default heap growth. It provides\nno basis for imposing a minimum heap or changing Gambit's evaluator.\n\nFor the orchestrator's shiva matrix, supply the actual source root explicitly:\n\n```sh\nmake gambityinrepl DATOMWORLD_ROOT=/home/sto/workspace/datomworld \\\n  GAMBIT_PREFIX=\"$HOME/.local/share/mise/installs/gambit/4.9.8\"\n```\n\nThe watchdog in the gate covers the whole session. The default-heap trace and\nfailure comparison are under `build/p1c-linux/`.\n\nOn macOS arm64, `gambityinrepl` passed before and after the preflight with the\nsame cached kernel and Datomworld `27f207c0`. Both watchdogged runs produced\nthe same 12 `yin>` replies byte for byte. `gambitsourceload` also passed.\n# P1c review findings — yin.repl under the jolt Gambit backend\n\nCompleted-GMT: 2026-11-20 03:2x:xx GMT\nCompleted-Local: 2026-11-20 10:2x:xx ICT (+07)\nCoding-Agent: glm (glm-5.3-flash)\nSession-ID: zcode-subagent-reviewer-p1c\nReviewed: gambit-ffi-p1c @ e28f40b6 (plus b77eea9a, f8741162), worktree /Users/sto/workspace/jolt-ffi-p1c\n\n## P1 — The gate is honest: VERIFIED\n\n`test/gambit/yin-repl-session.sh` is a genuine state-derived gate, not an echo check:\n\n- It drives the stock Yin entry (`host/gambit/yin-repl-main.ss` → `yin-repl-native.ss`\n  loads the compiled boot built from committed sources by `host/gambit/build-yin-boot.py`,\n  then `host/gambit/yin-repl-driver.ss` boots `jolt.gambit.yin` and calls the real\n  `yin.repl.main/-main` from the companion datomworld checkout).\n- The awk consumer (yin-repl-session.sh:34-48) is a strict 12-step ordered state machine\n  over `^yin> ` replies: `3`, `49`, `100`, `101` (arithmetic and a def/closure), `Error:\n  Divide by zero`, the `unavailable-parser: :yang/python` refusal (which must name the\n  installed `:clojure` frontend — a real catalog answer), `'jolt.ffi`, `4`\n  (`jolt.ffi/sizeof :int32` — a real FFI call result), `'dao.jing.mem`, the C4 blocking\n  message, `43` (proving the session survived the refusal), and `Bye`. Any nonzero process\n  status fails (lines 28-31); any unexpected `^yin> ` line sets `unexpected` and fails the\n  END condition (line 47). A broken REPL — crash, silence, wrong values, out-of-order\n  replies — fails. Exit status alone never passes (line 2).\n- Inputs are fed on stdin through `host/gambit/ffi/watchdog.sh` (2400s), which\n  preserves stdin, runs in a new session, and SIGKILLs the process group on timeout\n  (watchdog.sh:6-13). Watchdogged: yes.\n- Negative control exists in the receipts: `build/p1c-r3/yin-gate.log` (status 70,\n  \"a complete Yin session was not observed\") and `build/p1c-r3/yin-current.log`\n  (watchdog TIMEOUT at 2400s mid-load) show the gate failing on broken/incomplete\n  sessions during development. The failure mode is real, not theoretical.\n\n## Gate re-run (my own capture, darwin-arm64, Gambit 4.9.8 via mise)\n\n`GAMBIT_PREFIX=~/.local/share/mise/installs/gambit/4.9.8 make gambityinrepl` →\n**PASS**, reproducing the orchestrator capture line for line: `Host: jolt / Gambit\nv4.9.8`, `yin>` evaluations 3 / 49 / 100 / 101, `Error: Divide by zero`,\n`unavailable-parser: Yin REPL language :yang/python is not in the frontend catalog;\ninstalled: :clojure`, `'jolt.ffi`, `yin> 4`, `'dao.jing.mem`, the C4 blocking message\ninline, `yin> 43`, `yin> Bye`, and the \"published code index (project failed)\" warning\nclass on every round. Boot build + full session ran under the two 2400s watchdogs.\n\nStage-1 spot checks: `make gambitgencheck` / `gambitseedcheck` could not be re-run on\nthis machine — both run on Chez (`Makefile:1909-1940`) and no Chez is provisioned here\n(`.cache/local/chezscheme-10.4.1` missing); the failures I got are launch failures\nmisreported as \"STALE\"/\"cannot be minted\", not staleness. The author's green receipts\nfor both are in `build/p1c-r3/stage1.log` and `build/p1c-r3/matrix-final.log`\n(`gambitseedcheck: gambit seed is current`, `gambitgencheck: records-gambit.ss is\ncurrent`, plus gambitffi/gambitcheck/kernel-test/eval-test PASS). `unit-final.log` shows\nthe final 56-row unit run green including the SHA-256 refusal row.\n\n## P2 — C4 boundary in the session: VERIFIED\n\n- The inline refusal is the documented message, message-carrying not bare\n  (`host/gambit/scheme-adapter-runtime.ss:628-631`); identical text asserted in\n  yin-repl-session.sh:44 and `test/gambit/unit.edn:226-229` (refusal then `(+ 21 22)`\n  → 43 in the same session — survival asserted, and observed live).\n- `sa-foreign-procedure-blocking`, `sa-foreign-callable`,\n  `sa-foreign-callable-collect-safe` (foreign-thread) and runtime-signature construction\n  all raise documented refusals (scheme-adapter-runtime.ss:617-660). The local Dao hash\n  overlay (`host/gambit/yin/dao/host/hash.jolt`) supplies BLAKE3 in-process and routes\n  SHA-256 to the refusal at invocation, not load time. The subprocess/Python frontend\n  refuses as a catchable `unavailable-parser` diagnostic naming the installed catalog;\n  the session continues.\n- No claim of blocking / foreign-thread / dynamic-callable / Linux qualification\n  anywhere in the session, driver, or findings. The `sa-os-family` else-default `'linux`\n  is documented as a default, not a qualification (scheme-adapter-runtime.ss:255-262,\n  gambitcheck.ss:394). The qualified FFI tier remains the stage-1 registry only.\n\n## P3 — The three r2 fixes under session load: VERIFIED\n\n- Docstring emission: `jolt-core/jolt/backend_scheme/names.clj:22` joins the escaped\n  literal instead of one arg per character; `rt-core.ss` writes to a string port. The\n  `eval-test.ss` row builds a >9000-char doc with quotes, emoji, tab and trailing\n*** WARNING -- Variable \"var-cell-defined?-set!\" used in module \"kernel\" is undefined\n*** WARNING -- Variable \"var-cell-dyn-bound?\" used in module \"kernel\" is undefined\n*** WARNING -- Variable \"var-cell-dyn-bound?-set!\" used in module \"kernel\" is","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
